Installed dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

web/vendor/react-remove-scroll-bar/LICENSE preserves the upstream MIT notice
omitted from the react-remove-scroll-bar 2.3.8 npm tarball. It was copied from:
https://github.com/theKashey/react-remove-scroll-bar/blob/7301c160fda44cb8cf2b9fdfde61efad35736196/LICENSE

The frontend build emits licenses/NOTICE.txt with the installed frontend
packages' license notices, the Apache and MPL license texts, and the exact
Butai protocol helper source. These are linked from the design gallery.

Each installed dependency retains its own license. Notably three.js (MIT)
draws the viewport and build123d (Apache-2.0) provides the CAD API. Its CAD
kernel, Open CASCADE Technology, is LGPL-2.1 with the Open CASCADE exception:
https://dev.opencascade.org/doc/overview/html/occt_public_license.html

The dependency manifests are web/package.json and requirements.txt; the
resolved versions are in web/package-lock.json and requirements.lock.
Docker also installs the Butai daemon, agent CLIs and operating-system
packages. Caliper's Apache-2.0 license does not replace their terms. A
distributor of a built image must retain the applicable notices and satisfy
each component's source-availability and redistribution requirements.
